        timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. ABSOLUTE CATASTROPHIC WARNING: This is the infamous N47 timing chain. The lower chain guides are made of a defective material that wears prematurely, causing the chain to stretch, rattle, and eventually snap, destroying the engine. Replacing it requires a full engine removal. It MUST be monitored for a 'scraping' noise and replaced proactively before 150k km.)", injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection (Utilizes the notorious Bosch CP4 high-pressure fuel pump. The system provides excellent fuel efficiency, but the early CP4 pump is a known critical failure point that can send metal shrapnel throughout the entire fuel system, requiring a multi-thousand-euro replacement.)", engineLifespan: "250,000+ km (The mechanical aluminum block itself is strong, but the N47 is plagued by catastrophic peripheral failures. The rear-mounted timing chain snapping and the CP4 fuel pump disintegrating are two of the most expensive common failures in modern BMW history. Surviving past 250k km requires a massive proactive maintenance budget.)", turboType: "Turbocharged (Equipped with a single variable geometry turbocharger (VGT). It provides a decent 360Nm of torque off idle. The 143hp output is adequate for city driving but feels slightly breathless at highway speeds when passing in the heavy F25 chassis.)", ecuType: "Bosch DDE (A sophisticated digital diesel electronic system managing the common rail injection, VGT turbo, and DPF/EGR emissions. The ECU is highly tunable via OBD flashing, easily unlocking the hidden torque potential of this aluminum block.)", euroStandard: "Euro 5", maxPowerStockInternals: "180 - 190 hp (The N47 block is heavily over-engineered internally. A simple Stage 1 software tune safely unlocks roughly 185hp and 410Nm of torque, significantly improving the heavy SUV's acceleration without requiring any hardware modifications.)",
