          "CP4 High-Pressure Fuel Pump Failure: The Bosch CP4 pump is highly sensitive to fuel quality. It can disintegrate internally, sending metal glitter through the injectors and fuel lines, requiring a complete fuel system replacement.",
          "Intake Manifold Carbon Buildup & Swirl Flaps: The aggressive EGR system chokes the intake with thick carbon sludge. The plastic swirl flaps can also bind or break, throwing limp mode codes.",
          "EGR Cooler & Valve: The EGR valve frequently clogs with soot, and the EGR cooler can leak coolant internally, causing a fire hazard.",
          "DPF Clogging: The Diesel Particulate Filter will quickly clog with soot if driven strictly in urban environments, causing immense exhaust backpressure that destroys the turbocharger.",
          "Vibration Damper Degradation: The heavy main crankshaft pulley's rubber core cracks from absorbing vibrations, risking accessory belt failure.",
          "Glow Plug Module Failure: The glow plug control module fails frequently over high mileage, preventing cold starts and blocking mandatory DPF regeneration cycles."
